# Pre-existing, NOT introduced by this change: a SIGSEGV when the lock's
# parent directory cannot create the lock at all. fm_lock_try_acquire
# recurses into "$lockdir.steal" and keeps appending .steal until the shell
# stack overflows. Reproduced identically on the base commit and the target.

